{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":37.5,"text":"A bronze boxer sits with his elbows on his knees, turning his head as if someone had just called him, and he is worn out. On his hands he still wears the leather straps of the sport. His nose is broken, his ears are swollen, and the sculptor set pieces of red copper into the bronze to show the blood from his cuts. He was made between 330 and 50 BC. In 1885, he was found carefully buried on the Quirinal Hill, as if someone had wanted to save him. His toes and fingers are polished smooth. People in ancient times probably touched him for luck.","words":[{"word":"A","start":0,"end":0.47999998927116394},{"word":"bronze","start":0.47999998927116394,"end":0.7799999713897705},{"word":"boxer","start":0.7799999713897705,"end":1.2200000286102295},{"word":"sits","start":1.2200000286102295,"end":1.7400000095367432},{"word":"with","start":1.7400000095367432,"end":1.940000057220459},{"word":"his","start":1.940000057220459,"end":2.299999952316284},{"word":"elbows","start":2.299999952316284,"end":2.4800000190734863},{"word":"on","start":2.4800000190734863,"end":2.700000047683716},{"word":"his","start":2.700000047683716,"end":3.259999990463257},{"word":"knees","start":3.259999990463257,"end":3.259999990463257},{"word":"turning","start":4,"end":4},{"word":"his","start":4,"end":4.300000190734863},{"word":"head","start":4.300000190734863,"end":4.579999923706055},{"word":"as","start":4.579999923706055,"end":4.78000020980835},{"word":"if","start":4.78000020980835,"end":5},{"word":"someone","start":5,"end":5.28000020980835},{"word":"had","start":5.28000020980835,"end":5.460000038146973},{"word":"just","start":5.460000038146973,"end":5.900000095367432},{"word":"called","start":5.900000095367432,"end":5.900000095367432},{"word":"him","start":5.900000095367432,"end":6.119999885559082},{"word":"and","start":6.639999866485596,"end":6.71999979019165},{"word":"he","start":6.71999979019165,"end":6.920000076293945},{"word":"is","star